      "writtenOn": "2022-11-30T23:30:25Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Don\u0027t use environ to set / the `bArgs` value. We don\u0027t want to pollute the environment of other processes at all, and this isn\u0027t really an environment variable, which is what c.environ is used for.\n\nIt would be better to create a specific field \"buildCommandForMetrics\" or something of that nature.",
      "revId": "72170c77e88ba420fd130e8bedb07acecdcafe52",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "e5508064_4a1cae56",
        "filename": "ui/build/config.go",
        "patchSetId": 7
      },
      "lineNbr": 1162,
      "author": {
        "id": 1605027
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-11-30T23:30:25Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Why not, instead, you just treat a new field c.BuildCommand, as the source of truth? It\u0027s initialized to os.Args, but if you see a \"--build-command\" arg, then it overrides that field to the value of that flag?\n\nThat way you also don\u0027t need `SetBCommand`, because you will just set to the value of c.BuildCommand in metrics, without worrying about the origin of its value.",
      "revId": "72170c77e88ba420fd130e8bedb07acecdcafe52",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    }
